# Data card -- Wisconsin breast-cancer table (klein demo)

Written by the demo driver from the real prepared table and the real audit output below;
in a real study the DATA auditor writes every line from their own reading
(`references/data-gate-protocol.md`).

## Source & shape

`sklearn:load_breast_cancer` -- the Wisconsin diagnostic table, bundled with scikit-learn
(no network). One row per tumour sample: @@ROWS@@ rows x @@FEATURES@@ numeric features
(measurements of cell nuclei: radius, texture, perimeter, ... each as mean, error and
worst value) plus the label column `target` (1 = benign, 0 = malignant). The contract
carves it by a stratified split with seed @@SEED@@ into @@TRAIN@@ train, @@DEV@@
development and @@TEST@@ sealed rows; the sealed rows are never read before the one
confirmation run a real study would spend.

## Profile summary

Checked by value pattern, never by dtype:

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| numeric feature columns | @@FEATURES@@ of @@FEATURES@@ parse as finite floats |
| missing values | @@MISSING@@ |
| constant columns | @@CONSTANT@@ |
| label values | only 0 and 1; @@BENIGN@@ benign |
| row identifier or free text | none |

## Clean-room leakage audit

Run as `python -m kleinlib.leakage data/prepared/prepared.csv --target target --study .`:

```
@@LEAKAGE@@
```

Four rows, one verdict each: the split reproduces from the contract; no duplicate row
straddles two partitions; a constant predictor scores chance; a label-shuffled predictor
scores chance. All pass.

## Ranked go / no-go issues

1. **WARN -- small sample.** Only @@DEV@@ development rows: a score moves visibly when the
   partition is re-drawn. That is exactly what Phase 0 measures and what the keep bar
   will be built from.
2. **WARN -- strong, correlated features.** Radius, perimeter and area measure the same
   thing three ways, so a model can be very good and its coefficients will not be
   interpretable one by one. Fine for a ranking score, wrong for a causal reading.
3. **INFO -- a published, heavily studied table.** The headline AUC will be high for
   any reasonable model; the demo's point is the process around the number.
4. No BLOCKER found.

## Go / no-go

Nothing blocks modeling. The two warnings above travel with every claim a study on this
table makes.

> **Decision:** GO
